olar ] 21. Andreae MH, Dudak A, Cherian V, et al. Healthcare simulation to prepare for the COVID-19 pandemic. J Clin Anesth 2020; 66:109928. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22▪▪. Kuhn L, Lim ZJ, Flynn D, et al. Safety briefing and visual design key to protecting healthcare personnel during the COVID-19 pandemic. Am J Infect Control 2020; 48:1122–1124. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]; The authors present a model for education of healthcare workers in a pandemic. It includes clear and consistent messaging, and reinforces the need to consider all potential dangers to create a culture of safety and confidence. It also reinforces focus on healthcare worker wellness and teamwork. 23. Cag Y, Erdem H, Gormez A, et al. Anxiety among front-line health-care workers supporting patients with COVID-19: a global survey. Gen Hosp Psychiatry 2021; 68:90–96. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24▪. Norton EJ, Georgiou I, Fung A, et al. Personal protective equipment and infection prevention and control: a national survey of UK medical students and interim foundation doctors during the COVID-19 pandemic. J Public Health Oxf Engl 2021; 43:67–75. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]; The study found that students identifying as black, Asian, Minority Ethnic were less likely to report sufficient PPE availability and training and had higher anxiety regarding the pandemic. This study highlights the need for mental health and wellness resources for this group of healthcare workers. 25. Seliga R, Bhattacharya A, Succop P, et al. Effect of work load and respirator wear on postural stability, heart rate, and perceived exertion. Am Ind Hyg Assoc J 1991; 52:417–422. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Kempfle JS, Panda A, Hottin M, et al. Effect of powered air-purifying respirators on speech recognition among healthcare workers. Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg 2021; 164:87–90. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ 